WEBVTT

00:03:55.996 --> 00:04:00.996
allowing areal density to approach
one terabit per square inch.

00:04:01.204 --> 00:04:03.954
Recently, the potential limit
has been increased yet again

00:04:03.996 --> 00:04:07.663
through Heat Assisted Magnetic Recording.

00:04:08.538 --> 00:04:11.329
This uses an even more thermally
stable recording medium,

00:04:11.371 --> 00:04:14.204
whose magnetic resistance
is momentarily reduced

00:04:14.246 --> 00:04:16.954
by heating up a particular spot
with a laser

00:04:17.038 --> 00:04:19.704
and allowing data to be written.

00:04:20.288 --> 00:04:23.496
And while those drives are currently
in the prototype stage,

00:04:23.538 --> 00:04:26.704
scientists already have the next 
potential trick up their sleeves:

00:04:26.746 --> 00:04:29.288
bit-patterned media,

00:04:29.329 --> 00:04:33.371
where bit locations are arranged
in separate, nano-sized structures,